    prov:endedAtTime "2026-10-31T15:41:33Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

session:pr758Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #753 asked for docs/plans/LDP_PLAN.md: the plan-writing phase (per CLAUDE.md's TDD workflow) for epic #73, Linked Data Platform 1.0. Researched sparql_endpoint/src/graph_store.rs's existing direct-identification Graph Store Protocol routes (direct_gsp_get/put/post/delete/head under /rdf-graphs/{*path}) as the foundation, since LDP's URL-is-the-resource model matches GSP's direct model exactly. A first full draft was written from recall of the LDP 1.0 spec and reviewed with advisor() before being treated as final. The review caught that several normative claims (Allow/Accept-Post/ETag/constrainedBy section numbers, the PUT-containment-guard citation, and especially the pagination mechanism) were guessed rather than verified, and that out-of-scope items (Direct/Indirect Containers, LDP-NR, full paging conformance) had only been described in prose instead of filed as issues per CLAUDE.md's 'follow-up work discovered mid-task' rule. Fetched the actual W3C LDP 1.0 REC and the separate LDP Paging 1.0 Working Group Note (a distinct, non-normative document the core REC explicitly defers pagination to) and corrected every citation against the real text -- notably that ldp:pageSequence is a Link relation pointing at a sort-criteria resource, not an integer literal, and that paging request-side sizing uses Prefer: max-member-count=\"N\", not an invented include=\"...#Page\" syntax. Also grepped the codebase directly to confirm graph_store.rs emits none of Link/ETag/Allow/Accept-Post today and that no OPTIONS handler exists anywhere in sparql_endpoint, rather than assuming GSP's existing responses were partially reusable as-is." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:758 ;
    agp:decisionPoint session:pr758Decision ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr758 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .

session:pr758Decision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "Modeled each LDP container as one GSP named graph under the existing direct-identification route, whose stored triples are the container's own description plus the authoritative ldp:contains triples maintained transactionally by the POST/DELETE handlers -- keeping graph_store.rs completely untouched and pushing all LDP logic into a new sparql_endpoint/src/ldp.rs module that calls the existing parse/serialize/negotiate helpers." ;
    agp:alternative "Considered deriving ldp:contains at read time by scanning other graphs for a membership-indicating predicate, which would avoid storing containment state redundantly, but this conflates container membership with arbitrary application data and gives no natural place to enforce the spec's PUT-must-not-change-containment-triples rule (LDP 1.0 §5.2.4.1); rejected in favor of treating containment triples as server-managed state, same as GSP already treats a graph's own stored content." .
